From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:55:31 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 208/208] Meridian: Windows: a reopen after a crash too

As on macOS (0206): the browser process starts a watcher (meridian.exe itself,
--meridian-crash-watcher=<pid>, no windows) that waits on the browser's
process handle. If the browser ended without a clean exit (Default/Preferences
still says "exit_type":"Crashed"), no other Meridian holds the profile (its
lockfile), and there was no relaunch in the last two minutes, it starts
Meridian again. Only for an installed copy, and not under tests
(--remote-debugging-*, --headless, --meridian-test-*), unless
--meridian-crash-relaunch asks for it; =dry only writes
"<user data>/Meridian Crash Relaunch".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
